item+ function crates/phextron-web/src/json.rs :: Json::display :: pub fn display(&self) -> String { :: Display form, mirroring what the desktop shell's JS produces when it stringifies a JSON value into HTML: strings as themselves, booleans as `true`/`false`, null as empty (callers substitute the em dash where the JS does). Numbers go through their f64 value, because the JS shell stringifies the parsed number, not the wire lexeme: the server emits `8.0`, JSON.parse makes it `8`, and the shell shows `8` — so the WASM renderer shows `8` too. (Rust's `{}` for f64 is the same shortest-round-trip form JS uses at panel magnitudes.) :: direct :: api
item+ function crates/phextron-web/src/json.rs :: Json::get :: pub fn get(&self, key: &str) -> Option<&Json> { :: Function Json::get takes &self, key: &str. It gives back Option<&Json>. :: inferred :: api
